---
import LegalLayout from '~/layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '~/config/site';

export const prerender = true;
---

<LegalLayout
  title={`Terms & Conditions — ${site.name}`}
  description="The terms for using Khoobsurati — a free, no-account 90s Bollywood playlist site."
>
  <h1>Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
  <p class="updated">Last updated: August 11, 2026</p>

  <h2>1. Agreement</h2>
  <p>
    By using <strong>{site.domain}</strong>, you agree to these Terms. If you
    don't agree, please don't use the site. See also our
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>2. The service</h2>
  <p>
    Khoobsurati is a free, curated, looping playlist of 90s Bollywood songs,
    played in-browser via an embedded YouTube player, with links out to the
    same playlist on Spotify and YouTube Music. It's a hobby project, not a
    commercial streaming service, and it doesn't compete with or replace
    licensed music platforms.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Eligibility</h2>
  <p>
    Khoobsurati is intended for a general audience. If the law where you
    live requires a parent or guardian's permission for you to agree to
    website terms on your own, please use the site with that permission.
  </p>

  <h2>4. No accounts</h2>
  <p>
    No sign-up or account is required or offered. There's nothing to secure
    and no personal profile stored, so there's no account-security section
    here to worry about.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>Please don't:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Scrape, crawl, or automate requests to the site beyond normal browsing (including hammering the "online now" endpoint)</li>
    <li>Attempt to bypass, disable, or interfere with the site's security measures</li>
    <li>Use the site for anything illegal, or in a way that disrupts it for other listeners</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Content &amp; rights</h2>
  <p>
    Khoobsurati doesn't host, sell, or redistribute any audio itself. Playback
    happens entirely through YouTube's own embedded player, subject to
    <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">YouTube's Terms of Service</a>,
    and the playlist links point to Spotify and YouTube Music, each subject
    to their own terms. All song titles, recordings, artist names, film
    titles, and album artwork remain the property of their respective rights
    holders. The site's design, code, and curation are the operator's.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Copyright concerns</h2>
  <p>
    Since no media is hosted on {site.domain} itself, concerns about a
    specific recording should go to YouTube or Spotify directly. For
    anything about the site itself (a link that shouldn't be there, etc.),
    email <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Third-party services</h2>
  <p>
    The site relies on YouTube (playback embed), Spotify and YouTube Music
    (external playlist links), Google Analytics, and Cloudflare — each
    governed by its own terms and privacy policy, linked in the
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>9. No warranty</h2>
  <p>
    The site is provided free of charge, "as is" and "as available," on a
    best-effort basis, with no guarantee of uptime, availability, or that
    playback will always work. Features — including the "online now" counter
    — may change, break, or be discontinued at any time without notice.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the maximum extent permitted by law, the operator isn't liable for
    any damages arising from your use of, or inability to use, the site.
    Some jurisdictions don't allow the exclusion or limitation of certain
    warranties or liabilities — in those cases, this limitation applies only
    to the extent the law allows.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    These Terms may be updated from time to time; changes will be posted
    here with a new "Last updated" date. Continued use of the site after
    changes are posted means you accept the revised Terms.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These Terms are governed by the laws of the jurisdiction in which the
    operator resides, without regard to conflict-of-laws principles. Where a
    dispute can't be brought there, both parties consent to the courts with
    jurisdiction over the operator as the alternate forum.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these Terms:
    <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
